I think it's because of the recursive fft function above. In this code am using a for loop for a parallel FFT that runs in O(logN). It now consumes around 100% CPU with OpenMP. Not yet optimized (still contains a lot of unnecessary memory allocations, but it runs much faster now than Python). Didn't know that OpenMP is sensitive with the type of function in its threads. #include <iostream>
