answers.body:
You're trying to pass a number from one function ( bar or find_pivot ) to its caller ( foo or quicksort ). Using a global variable is a bad pattern for that. Change your tests that do not allow you to do that. Trying to work around that gives you unreadable, unmaintainable, and just painfully complicated code. In fact, it makes it so uselessly complicated that you can't even figure out how to write it yourself while the alternates are very simple. Compare this: int find_pivot(int *arr, int low, int high)
{
    return ...;
}

void quicksort(int *arr, int low, int high)
{
    ...
    int pivot_index = find_pivot(arr, low, high);
    quicksort(arr, low, pivot_index - 1);
    quicksort(arr, pivot_index + 1, high);
} Or using a pointer (typically if you have several values, or a complex value, to return): void find_pivot(int *arr, int low, int high, int *pivot_index)
{
    *pivot_index = ...;
}

void quicksort(int *arr, int low, int high)
{
    ...
    int pivot_index = -1;
    find_pivot(arr, low, high, &pivot_index);
    quicksort(arr, low, pivot_index - 1);
    quicksort(arr, pivot_index + 1, high);
} With the following (wrong!), which is close to what you have written: int pivot_index;

