#pragma omp critical(push_in_relevant_points)
                     relevant_points.push_back(pointcloud[i]);
                 }
            }
        }
} I used mop critical instead of guard_lock for more consistency and i did a reserve at the beginning.
Because in my case the relevant_points vector is never going to be bigger than point cloud and most of the time he contain only 50 to 100 elements. And i'm not using a copy of the vector anymore but a reference.

