How exactly does it fail? Have you tried just e.g. printing the thread number to see if n_threads is spawned? If you are "just" getting wrong results in the intersection_points and cell_ids , that is because those arrays are reset by each thread whenever they enter the IntersectWithLine function (you can look at the implementation here , lines 800-808). To solve this, the easiest solution that comes to mind is have each thread have it's own list and then concatenate them in a critical section, but faster will probably be pre-allocating array of those list for each thread and then reading the results from it, e.g.: vtkSmartPointer<vtkPoints> *inter_points = new vtkSmartPointer<vtkPoints> [n_threads];
