answers.body:
Just decouple the loops.  If your current code is #pragma omp parallel for
for(int i = 0; i < 5; ++i)
{
  expensive_1(i);
  for(int j = 0; j < 5; ++j)
  {
    expensive_2(j);
  }
} then make it into this, possibly saving the results of expensive_1 if they are needed in expensive_2 . #pragma omp parallel for
for(int i = 0; i < 5; ++i)
{
  expensive_1(i);
}

#pragma omp parallel for collapse(2)
for(int i = 0; i < 5; ++i)
{
  for(int j = 0; j < 5; ++j)
  {
    expensive_2(j);
  }
}

